Related Work
\subsection{Deepfake detection}

Deepfake detection can be broadly divided into two categories: model based and model free detection. In model based detection, the deepfake detection is performed by training machine learning models on handcrafted features extracted from the deepfake videos. The handcrafted features can be either visual or audio based. In model free detection, the deepfake detection is performed directly on the raw input video without using any handcrafted features. 

\subsection{Model based detection}

Model based detection methods use machine learning models to classify whether a given video is a deepfake or not. The machine learning models can be either supervised or unsupervised. Supervised models are trained on labelled data while unsupervised models are trained on unlabelled data. Supervised models typically perform better than unsupervised models but require more labelled data for training. 

\subsection{Model free detection}

Model free detection methods perform deepfake detection directly on the raw input video without using any handcrafted features. These methods typically use deep learning models such as convolutional neural networks (CNNs) or recurrent neural networks (RNNs) to classify whether a given video is a deepfake or not. <|section_end|>

