\subsection{Multi-modal Inference}
Multi-modal reasoning aims to infer the relationship between the source image(s) and textual clues. The canonical formulation usually take the source image(s) as the input and request the inference model to perform a multi-choice classification according to the textual query. The query is usually in the form of a question, a statement, or a sentence with a blank to be filled. The multi-modal inference tasks can be further divided into two categories. One is to infer the relationship between the source image(s) and a single textual clue, such as visual question answering \cite{arxivID-2010.08708-8}

