 Cancer is one of the leading causes of death worldwide and accurate diagnosis, staging and restaging are essential to optimize therapeutic management. Advanced medical imaging techniques such as positron emission tomography (PET) coupled with computed tomography (CT) are integral for clinical assessment of cancer diagnosis, and assessment of treatment response. PET is the most sensitive non-invasive imaging modality capable of detecting picomolar amounts of radiolabeled  glucose, which is taken up by glucose metabolizing cells. PET/CT is the standard of care for staging and restaging of cancer patients. \cite{arxivID-1603.02900-0, arxivID-1705.07062-1, arxivID-1702.02223-2}

