The domain shift problem is particularly noticeable at class boundaries, where the network tends to produce blurry predictions. This is a critical problem for semantic segmentation, since the main goal of this task is to obtain sharp boundaries between different classes. Moreover, such problem is exacerbated in the context of domain adaptation, where the domain shift is larger.

